@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@
+# arch(egress): store-and-forward queue migration (ratified spine 2026-08-26)
+
+THE model migration: the packet flow re-keys from the undirected
+per-(bundle, lane) queue to the **(router, egress-port, lane)** port queue —
+store-and-forward egress QoS, per the ratified architecture spine
+`_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/architecture-egress-qos-2026-08-26/ARCHITECTURE-SPINE.md`
+(4/4 user rulings adopted 2026-08-26: R1 full duplex, R2 per-pipe weights
+panel, R3 no propagation, R4 per-(port,lane) bound 6).
+
+## The story ladder (one commit per story, suite green between)
+
+| Story | Law | What |
+|---|---|---|
+| S1 | AD-2/D2 | The port identity: `(router, egress-port, lane)` where egress-port = the directional bundle; PHYSICAL ENCODING STAYS DERIVED (on_edge/edge/at_node — no new Packet field). The retained departure node `at_node` is CANONICAL for the port's router; the heading derivation coincides by construction (pinned). Semantics-preserving: 49/49 demos byte-identical, zero re-bless. |
+| S2 | AD-5/R1 | **FULL DUPLEX**: each direction gets its own `bundle_cap` serve budget (a 1 Gbps link is 1 Gbps each way). Tx utilization ring per (bundle, direction). Enumeration (bundle asc, heading asc) pinned (AV-3). |
+| S3 | D-2 (the named story) | `bandwidth_demand` WIRED into the AD-3(c) serialization term: `need = demand(class) × packet_bandwidth` (email 800, streaming 1600). |
+| S4 | AD-4/R4 + AV-1/2 + F1 | E9 drop ladder + crisis engine + pipe warnings re-keyed to the port, semantics VERBATIM. `Packet_Dropped.target` STAYS the bundle id (AV-1); the port's direction rides the existing tag-conditional `Event.direction` slot for drop + crisis tags (AV-2). Cooldown key gains the direction bit (F1: A→B resolve ≠ B→A re-fire). |
+| S5 | AD-3/F2 + AV-5 + AD-7/F3 | The latency ledger (per-(port,lane,class) rolling residency accumulators, exact F2 term split) + the reads contract: `router_buffering_packets`, `port_util_pct`, `port_residency_ticks`; stats v3 Q rows per (router, port); NOC QUEUE DEPTH re-key; qos_panel per-direction depths. |
+
+## Balance disclosures (deliberate, disclosed per the rulings)
+
+- **S2 — full duplex**: bidirectional-shared pairs gain **2× effective serve
+  capacity** (each direction drains at the full bundle_cap; reverse streams no
+  longer compete for the forward budget). Same-direction estate contention
+  survives.
+- **S3 — D-2 demand wiring**: streaming transit **8→16 ticks** at the standard
+  tier (ceil(1600/100)); 32 ticks on era-3-decayed legacy standard; 1 tick on
+  mid/wide (unchanged). Streaming SLA math shifts everywhere standard-path
+  streaming contends (2-hop shorts now 1650 ms > the 1200 ms tolerance —
+  fixtures re-staged on a 1-hop recovery path). Email unchanged (demand 1).
+- **S4 — bound re-scope (R4/F4)**: the E9 lane bound is per (port, lane) —
+  per-pair buffer capacity doubles (**6→12 packets per lane per pair**),
+  accepted with the ruling.
+
+## T1/T2 re-bless inventory (deliberate, per golden discipline)
+
+- **S2 (16 demos)**: `a11y_{deutan,protan,tritan,scale,reduced} warn qos
+  qos_contention juice terminal_types advance_block_legacy advance_fire audio
+  legacy_decay node_health sla` — the first tick a bundle carries both
+  directions' packets in one lane shifts serve interleaving. Unidirectional
+  runs byte-identical BY CONSTRUCTION (33 demos untouched).
+- **S3 (24 demos)**: the S2 set + `health_lose forecast_preview surge pause
+  era_advance qos_emphasis qos_manual qos_auto` — standard-path streaming
+  transits doubled. Fat-pipe streaming demos (`estate_surge growth
+  dublin_*`) byte-identical (1-tick transit under any demand).
+- **S4 (23 demos)**: every drop/crisis-emitting run — the +1 direction
+  payload byte shifts the event-stream fold of the T1 hash + the bound
+  re-scope's behavioral shifts.
+- **S5**: ZERO drift (all derived state).
+- Union across the branch: **26 `.t1` + 44 T2 pngs** re-blessed.
+
+## The D6 proof (LOG_VERSION stays 6)
+
+- `LOG_VERSION :: u32(6)` — unchanged.
+- **Every `.log.bin` is byte-identical to `origin/v2`** (0 changed across the
+  branch): the action log is commands; every run replays under the same
+  command stream.
+- The serialized crises section is byte-pinned unchanged (31/row —
+  `Active_Crisis.dir` is derived engine memory, never serialized).
+- Save/replay: the replay gate green on 49/49 demos at head
+  (`harness replay surge` — 4000 ticks bit-for-bit); the determinism suite
+  (log round-trip) green.
+- All new state (residency ledger, serviced scratch, tx ring split, cooldown
+  dir, Drop_Site dir) is DERIVED — replay rebuilds identically.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `odin test core` 276 · `odin test app` 48 · `odin test app/render` 100 —
+  all green. New pins: directional split/invisibility (S1), full-duplex
+  independence + single-direction-unchanged (S2), streaming 16-tick transit +
+  per-class frac + mixed FIFO (S3), per-port bound admit/shed + AV-1/2
+  payload + F1 cooldown key (S4), F2 (b)=7 residency exactness + port rows +
+  reads (S5).
+- **Mutation legs RED-then-GREEN per story** (the house bar): S1 direction
+  filter bypass; S2 shared-budget collapse (6/12 arrived at tick 50); S3
+  demand unwired (streaming arrives 9 not 17); S4 pooled bound; S5 record
+  pass deleted ((b) reads 0).
+- Harness: 49 demos green (stability-checked ×3), palcheck green,
+  drift-check 353/353 rejected, stats-check live==replay byte-identical
+  (estate_surge, qos_contention, surge, spawn_feel).
+- Tuned fixtures re-staged with measured comments: sla breach/exit (1-hop
+  recovery; email follower 33 ticks behind the jumbo — 17 queues on e2/e3),
+  health E16/refill/no-soft-lock (expiry pinned 427, death 477, F-swept
+  220..300), crisis shed-site 0→2, w11 aggregation (W 1200 + host 200),
+  palcheck puck-LED floor, stats congested re-pins per story.
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **AV-1 vs the briefing one-liner**: the briefing's S4 summary line "drop
+  events target = port" reads lossy — the spine (LAW) is explicit and was
+  implemented: `Packet_Dropped.target` STAYS the bundle id; the port resolves
+  at the read site from target + the direction payload byte.
+- **Crisis display naming**: the (router, port) name resolves at read time
+  from the serialized pair + the event's direction payload (the spine's AV-2
+  amendment). The visual naming lands with the link-vocab render heists; the
+  payload + row machinery is complete here.
+- **Count-based measures stay count-based** (warnings pressure, node-health
+  load, stats `carried/offered`): S3's scope is the AD-3(c) serialization
+  formula (the briefing's letter); demand-weighting the congestion reads is a
+  render/balance follow-up, not this migration. Documented here so it's a
+  decision, not an oversight.
+- **P-row util = MAX over directions** (AV-4): the denominator is ALWAYS the
+  per-direction cap; a bidirectional pair at 100% each way reads 100, never
+  200. `tx_octets` is a counter (Σ both directions — honest octets).
+- **The shadow_clone incident** (fixed in-place): the S5 Flow_State arrays
+  were initially missing from `spawn_fx.odin`'s `shadow_clone` — the
+  spawn-feel prediction shadow carried the LIVE state's pointers and
+  corrupted them (heap abort at `run_destroy`, caught via
+  `malloc_error_break` backtrace; the tx-ring comment in the same proc
+  documents the identical prior incident). Cloned like every other
+  step()-touched dynamic; `flow_init` now makes the ledger arrays (cap 1) so
+  destroys are always over live allocations (the mirror-fixture rule).
+- **Node-stuck measure unchanged**: at-node unadmitted stuck packets remain
+  the separate 4.1 telegraph (AV-6) — never folded into router buffering.
+- **Rejected**: re-keying `Packet_Dropped.target` to a port id (AV-1 blocker
+  — old-read compat + no LOG_VERSION bump); serializing the ledger (D6 —
+  derived state keeps replay a pure function); per-delivered-packet
+  attribution (AV-5 — per-hop routing carries no route history).
+
+## Canon note (the standing bmad-build waiver)
+
+Per the standing Silas ruling (2026-08-21, reaffirmed 2026-08-23 — ×6+
+sightings): bmad-build's render fails on this install (ambiguous config token
+`implementation_artifacts` + no `render_skill.py` in `_bmad/scripts/`), so
+the skill is WAIVED for this job; this self-contained briefing + the
+step-04-equivalent review swarm (adversarial-general + edge-case-hunter
+lenses, findings verified against disk) carried the workflow.
+
+Closes the migration the spine gates; the link-vocab render heists consume
+the AD-7 reads contract this PR ships.
